.rss .notice { border: 1px solid #b26b00; color: #7a4a00; padding: 3px 6px; margin: 4px 0 8px; }
.rss table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 8px 0; }
.rss th, .rss td { border: 1px solid #555; padding: 3px 4px; text-align: start; vertical-align: top; }
.rss th { background: #eee; }
.rss .sign { margin-top: 24px; }
</style>
<div class="rss" dir="{{ 'rtl' if is_rtl() else 'ltr' }}">
<h1>{{ book.title|e }}{% if book.form %} <span class="fine">({{ book.form|e }})</span>{% endif %}: purchaser's slip</h1>
<div class="fine">{{ book.cite|e }}</div>
{%- if not book.certified %}<div class="notice">{{ _("A starting point, not certified for the country. Check each column against the instrument before you rely on it.")|e }}</div>{% endif %}
<p>{{ (doc.company or "")|e }} · {{ doc.name|e }} · {{ (doc.posting_date or "")|e }} · {{ (doc.customer_name or doc.customer or "")|e }}</p>
{%- if doc.docstatus == 2 %}
<p>This sale was cancelled: its entries are corrected in the {{ book.title|e }}, and it has no purchaser's slip.</p>
{%- elif doc.is_return %}
<p>A return has no purchaser's slip: the {{ book.title|e }} records it as a return.</p>
{%- elif lines %}
<table>
<thead><tr><th>{{ _("No.")|e }}</th><th>{{ _("Item")|e }}</th><th>{{ _("Lot")|e }}</th><th>{{ _("Quantity")|e }}</th><th>{{ _("Date")|e }}</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{%- for l in lines %}
<tr><td>{{ l.number }}</td><td>{{ (l.item_name or "")|e }}</td><td>{{ (l.batch_no or "")|e }}</td><td>{{ "%g"|format(l.qty or 0) }} {{ (l.uom or "")|e }}</td><td>{{ (l.entry_date or "")|e }}</td></tr>
{%- endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
{%- if lines|length == 200 %}<p>This slip lists the sale's first 200 entries in the book.</p>{% endif %}
<p>I received the items above, entered in the {{ book.title|e }} under the numbers shown.</p>
<p class="sign">Signature of purchaser ______________________________ Date ______________</p>
<p class="sign">Supplied by (name and signature) ______________________________</p>
{%- else %}
<p>This sale has no entry in the {{ book.title|e }} that you may read. A slip is printed for a sale the book took, signed in, after the sale is submitted; a sale delivered later books on its delivery, which has no slip.</p>
{%- endif %}
</div>

